Z||000000||Knight Rider||07-25-2001||04:32 PM||||I have been lurking around the Fiero Forum for a couple of weeks getting familiar with it and seeing what it was like.  I am getting a second car and I like the looks of the Fiero.  At one time I was looking at a 95 Mustang, but I wanted something unique and was small but safe and the body panels would not rust out after a few years.  Besides my other car that I am replacing is a old ricer (85 Honda Accord).  I wanted to get some advice from the forum members as to my selection of a Fiero model.<P>I am going to look for a 1988 GT or Formula with an automatic and 6 cyl. engine.  Then later rebuild a 3.1 or 3.4 and drop in place of the 2.8.  Is there anything I should be aware when looking?  Also, I like the thought of a 1989 Fiero kit, it would be the only kit that I would consider doing.  ||||reg||5
